TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress — launch/orbit tasks planned and course astrodynamics mentioned, but no actual orbit/launch analysis applied yet"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress — STK selected ('STK Design', 'STK Simulations', tutorials completed)"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1 — Gantt chart with weekly schedule and task descriptions"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Useful Links — list of planned information sources"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress — research and STK tutorials done, but no preliminary technical results presented"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"No explicit mission requirements, orbit, or payload specifications are stated; the sensing approach (Asner's airborne spectroscopy) is proposed for a satellite without discussing adaptation feasibility (e.g. spatial resolution, cloud cover limitations for optical reef monitoring)."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"Gantt chart shows 'STK Simulations' starting in Week 4 before design stages, which is plausible but unexplained; no schedule contingency/slack is included."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"No quantitative preliminary work (e.g. altitude/coverage estimates, hand calculations) despite claiming near-real-time relay, which drives orbit constellation choices."}],"overall":"A well-presented, clearly written preliminary report with a compelling Australia-focused mission concept, a detailed Gantt-based plan, and cited sources. Weakened by absent formal mission requirements, no contingency planning, and preliminary progress limited to tutorials and reading rather than technical results.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Clear mission purpose (GBR bleaching monitoring), identified users (marine/conservation scientists), and strong motivation with cited literature. However, no explicit mission goals, objectives, or requirements are formally stated, and payload/sensor specifics are only implied via Asner's technology.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Reef-monitoring satellites could also be used to report sea surface temperatures, thermal stress on coral, and bathymetry"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":18.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"Detailed Gantt chart with weekly tasks, deadlines, and per-task descriptions tied to the mission (launch, orbit, ground control, comms). Information sources listed. However, no contingency or provision for variations is described, which the Accomplished descriptor requires.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart. Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Week 10 is reserved for review, amendments, final simulations, and reflection."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Progress is limited to background research and STK tutorials; no preliminary technical results (orbit parameters, coverage calcs, simulations output) are presented or interpreted. Fits 'minor work completed' with insufficient results description.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4"},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have read the brief of Asner's monitoring system in Hawaii, researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity"}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":14.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Well-written, logical structure with clear headings, consistent formatting, footnoted references matching source list, and an explained, legible Gantt chart. Minor flaws: 'Useful Links' are not cited in text, and the Gantt figure lacks a numbered caption, keeping it at the lower Accomplished bound.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Oceans have become 30 percent more acidic since the industrial revolution leading to the bleaching of coral reefs."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Completed stages are gold. Incomplete stages are blue. Deadlines are indicated by red lines."}]}]}
